{"_meta":{"openai/outputTemplate":"ui://widget/clypmint-video.html","openai/widgetAccessible":true,"securitySchemes":[{"scopes":["clypmint"],"type":"oauth2"}],"ui":{"resourceUri":"ui://widget/clypmint-video.html"}},"annotations":{"destructiveHint":true,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":false,"title":"Edit scenes directly"},"description":"Apply exact edits without a Clypmint model round. Read get_project_context first. Canvas ops: output_frame {frame: {ratio: 9:16, 16:9, 1:1 or 4:5, fit}} reshapes this video (\"make it vertical\"); fit subject (the default) follows the subject, contain keeps the whole picture with bars (only when they ask to fit or keep everything in), cover fills; optional x/y (0-1, with fit cover only) move the centre of the filled frame; add: true makes the shape an extra output and keeps this one (\"a square version too\"); frame: null alone (no second op) is the original shape again (\"undo the crop\"); layout moves/scales/rotates a returned element ID using its units; element changes supported text/color/hidden; put_overlay adds or updates timed text/images with none/fade/slide/pop animation; remove_overlay removes an added element. Use only returned editable capabilities and existing canvas image assetIds. These are the manual editor operations and preserve authored animation. Music: {op:\"music\",enabled:false} removes only added music; enabled:true with track (one of Clypmint's own tracks, never claimed when posted: bright-house (upbeat), lofi-desk (calm), tech-forward (tech), documentary-pulse (story), gym-phonk (energetic), acoustic-morning (warm), soft-piano (emotional), funk-pop (fun), night-suspense (mystery), rise-up (inspiring)) or with music_staging_key from import_asset (a song of their own). Optional level_db (-36 to 0 relative to source audio) and beat_sync:true for source-shot action montages; other editing clocks refuse beat sync explicitly. Scene ops: remove, remove_layer, replace_screen, set_text, swap_picture (an existing picture key), move, add, cut_words, emphasis, captions, sound, scene_sounds. remove and cut_words take footage time out of the video; to delete a graphic and keep the footage and captions under it use remove_layer {layer: graphic}, to delete a zoom or camera move remove_layer {layer: camera}, and to shorten or lengthen a graphic move its scene to fewer or more words. scene_sounds replaces the scene cue list (empty removes added cues): choose names from scenes.soundOptions, optional on from soundWords.index and gain -36 to -10 dB. It preserves speech; global sound mute still applies. Batch up to 40 ops: all apply or all refuse. Native canvas changes save a playable project; export separately for a video file. Older timeline operations may require rendering; unsupported native operations refuse without rebuilding the project. Set base_version and output_id from context. Hook openings use revise_video. Free, up to 30 a day. Preserve operation_id and exact arguments on retries. Cost: Free: no credits.","inputSchema":{"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#","additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"base_version":{"description":"The version the edits are for; the current one when left out.","maxLength":200,"minLength":1,"type":"string"},"operation_id":{"description":"A stable ID for this request. Preserve it on retries. Use a new ID only for a deliberate new request.","pattern":"^[a-zA-Z0-9_.:-]{1,100}$","type":"string"},"ops":{"items":{"anyOf":[{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"op":{"const":"remove","type":"string"},"scene_id":{"description":"A scene id (sceneId) from get_project_context.","maxLength":120,"minLength":1,"type":"string"}},"required":["op","scene_id"],"type":"object"},{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"layer":{"enum":["graphic","camera"],"type":"string"},"op":{"const":"remove_layer","type":"string"},"scene_id":{"description":"A scene id (sceneId) from get_project_context.","maxLength":120,"minLength":